    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1972-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The condition \\(\\lvert x-2\\rvert\\le7\\) gives \\(-5\\le x\\le9.\\) The condition \\(\\lvert x-2\\rvert\\ge1\\) gives \\(x\\le1\\) or \\(x\\ge3.\\) Their intersection is \\[ [-5,1]\\cup[3,9]. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "The upper bound places \\(x\\) within \\(7\\) units of \\(2\\)",
        "The lower bound removes the open interval of points less than \\(1\\) unit from \\(2\\)"
      ],
